From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: feed the watchdog's hosc from the DCXO

The watchdog node from `watchdog-sunxi-a733-add-wdt0` names SYS_CLK24M as its high-frequency input
("hosc"). The A733's WDT does not count from that net.

WHERE EACH VALUE COMES FROM

  * A733 UM 8.3.3: the WDT counts from either CLK_32K or the DCXO
    divided by 750 (26 MHz / 750), selected by WDT_CFG_REG bit[8]
    (0: RTC_32K, 1: DCXO/750, UM 8.3.6.5).
  * The DCXO is exported by the RTC-CCU as CLK_RTC_DCXO (patch `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-rtc-ccu-add-dcxo`). Its
    rate was read at the register on silicon: XO_CTRL0[15:14] = 0b10 =
    26 MHz (2026-07-22).
  * `watchdog-sunxi-a733-add-wdt0` could not point there because no DCXO provider existed when it
    was written; its own comment asked for this change once one did.

A523 VALUE REJECTED: sun55i-a523.dtsi gives its watchdog <&osc24M> as
hosc. On the A733 the high-frequency source is the DCXO, not SYS_CLK24M.

WHAT THIS CHANGES AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

  * sunxi_wdt never calls clk_get(), so no rate is consumed and the
    watchdog's timing cannot change through this phandle.
  * fw_devlink turns the phandle into a supplier link: the watchdog now
    probes only after the RTC-CCU. That is the one runtime effect, and it
    matters: U-Boot arms WDT0 for 16 s (the U-Boot patch `sunxi-cubie-a7s-watchdog-autostart`) and only
    sunxi_wdt's probe stops it -- measured 2026-09-13:
    a kernel without that probe was reset by the U-Boot watchdog before
    `reboot` ran. The RTC-CCU is built in (SUN60I_A733_RTC_CCU=y) and already
    supplies the CPU-PLL CCU.

VERIFIED HERE: applies with fuzz 0 on top of the full series; the dtb,
built with cpp + dtc, decompiles to clocks = <rtc_ccu 2>, <osc32k>.

VERIFIED ON HARDWARE (2026-09-13, test build of this patch): the live DT
carries clocks = <0x22 2>, <0x1e> with 0x22 = clock-controller@7090000;
sunxi-wdt probes at 1.25 s with nothing deferred and an active supplier
link to 7090000.clock-controller (none without this patch); /dev/watchdog
appears, the board runs past 16 s, and an opened, never-fed /dev/watchdog
sets MODE 0xB1 and resets the board to BOOT0 about 17 s later (16 s
interval plus reset and measurement slack, not separated).

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -973,22 +973,21 @@
 		 *        the register layout, not the interrupt map.
 		 * clocks UM 8.3.3: the WDT's two selectable sources are RTC_32K
 		 *        and DCXO/750, picked by WDT_CFG_REG bit[8]. "losc" is
-		 *        therefore exactly right, and it is the selected one on
-		 *        silicon (WDT_CFG bit8 = 0 on both 6 GiB boards, 2026-07-22).
-		 *        "hosc" is the closest approximation the DT can express
-		 *        today: the real high-frequency source is the 26 MHz
-		 *        DCXO, not the 24 MHz SYS_CLK24M this node names, and
-		 *        no DCXO clock provider exists on this branch. The
-		 *        driver reads neither rate (sunxi_wdt never calls
-		 *        clk_get), so nothing computes on it -- but re-point
-		 *        "hosc" at the RTC-CCU's DCXO once that lands.
+		 *        the RTC_32K input and the one selected on silicon
+		 *        (WDT_CFG bit8 = 0, read on two boards 2026-07-22 and
+		 *        again 2026-09-13). "hosc" is the 26 MHz DCXO, exported
+		 *        by the RTC-CCU as CLK_RTC_DCXO (patch `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-rtc-ccu-add-dcxo`) -- not the
+		 *        24 MHz SYS_CLK24M the A523 dtsi uses. The driver reads
+		 *        neither rate (sunxi_wdt never calls clk_get); what the
+		 *        phandle does change is probe order, because fw_devlink
+		 *        makes the RTC-CCU a supplier of this node (patch `arm64-dts-a733-feed-the-watchdog-hosc-from-the-dcxo`).
 		 */
 		wdt: watchdog@2050000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-wdt",
 				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-wdt";
 			reg = <0x0 0x02050000 0x0 0x20>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 106 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-			clocks = <&osc24M>, <&osc32k>;
+			clocks = <&rtc_ccu CLK_RTC_DCXO>, <&osc32k>;
 			clock-names = "hosc", "losc";
 		};
 
